            <div xml:id="d223">

                <pb facs="0511" n="472" sameAs="frus:frus1981-88v24/pg472"/>

                <head>223. Memorandum From Secretary of State Shultz to President Reagan<anchor n="1" xml:id="d223-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1984-03-01">March 1, 1984</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>[Omitted here is material unrelated to Morocco.]</p>
                <p>4. <hi rendition="#italic">Morocco: Official Visit of the Prime Minister.</hi>
                    Prime Minister Karim-Lamrani and I met late this afternoon to summarize the
                    results of his visit.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d223-f2"/> We have signed a major
                    agreement, for expansion of the existing Voice of America broadcast facility,
                    and initialed another, a bilateral investment treaty. We have found additional
                    funds for FY 84 PL–480 and have restored some FMS
                    credits. I believe we have been successful in reassuring the Moroccans of our
                    commitment to develop assistance programs in FY
                    85 and FY 86 which take Morocco’s great needs
                    into account. (S)</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d223-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d223-f1-content">
